There are reasons why Americans never learn foreign languages, and one of 
the main ones is that the textbooks present us with the most stultifying 
versions possible.  I learned far more German trying to read a one chapter 
of a German astronomy textbook with a dictionary than I did in a year of 
classroom German.

I still have memorized part of a dialogue from my German class from 
1968.  It is wonderful should I ever be a student asking another about 
going with them to the library to return a book.  Something I doubt that I 
ever did in English even (what - I need an escort to walk to the library now?).

